{"park":"gateway_arch","fetched":"2026-09-06T17:49:35+00:00","attribution":{"landmarks":"© OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL","summaries":"Wikipedia, CC BY-SA 4.0","boundary":"iNaturalist place 137962"},"landmarks":[{"id":"relation/12813920","name":"Gateway Arch","kind":"attraction","lon":-90.18497,"lat":38.62461,"ele_m":null,"wikidata":"Q45234","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gateway_Arch","tour":0,"summary":{"extract":"The Gateway Arch is a 630-foot-tall (192 m) monument in St. Louis, Missouri, United States. Clad in stainless steel and built in the form of a weighted catenary arch, it is the world's tallest arch and Missouri's tallest accessible structure. Some sources consider it the tallest human-made monument in the Western Hemisphere. Built as a monument to the westward expansion of the United States and officially dedicated to \"the American people\", the Arch, commonly referred to as \"The Gateway to the West\", is a National Historic Landmark in Gateway Arch National Park and has become a popular tourist destination, as well as an internationally recognized symbol of St. Louis.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gateway_Arch","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/49/St._Louis_Gateway_Arch_-_panoramio.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St._Louis_Gateway_Arch_-_panoramio.jpg","dist_m":1,"width":640,"height":853,"license":"CC BY 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","artist":"Jim Bowen"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/GatewaySL4.jpg/960px-GatewaySL4.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GatewaySL4.jpg","dist_m":7,"width":640,"height":480,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","artist":"Cdv1014"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/St._Louis_Gateway_Arch_5.jpg/960px-St._Louis_Gateway_Arch_5.jpg","page":